__tablestorage__/

# ---- Secrets (never commit) ----
appsettings.*.Local.json
secrets.json
*.env
.env
.env.*

# Local scratch notes — has held pasted secrets (keys/connection strings); keep out of git.
NOTES.md

# The working to-do list. Personal, churns constantly, and belongs to whoever is at the keyboard
# rather than to the repository — it was tracked from Stage 1 to the docs cleanup, which is long
# enough that it needs a rule and not just a deletion, or the next `git add -A` puts it straight
# back. What is actually planned lives in PROJECT.md; what is in flight lives in the branch.
TODO.md

# ---- Python (voice bridge) ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
voice-bridge/.venv/
voice-bridge/.env
voice-bridge/models/
voice-bridge/voices/
# …but the template is safe to track (the .env.* rule above would otherwise catch it):
!voice-bridge/.env.example

# ---- Node / client ----
node_modules/
client/dist/
client/.vite/
client/coverage/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Build output served by API ----
# The whole directory, not a list of the things `npm run build` happens to put in it. It was
# `assets/` + `index.html` until the icon pack arrived and added `icons/` and `favicon.ico` — and
# enumerating build output is how a copied artefact ends up committed, which is the same trap the
# dev-CA rule below already documents. Nothing in here is source: `vite build` writes it with
# `emptyOutDir`, so every build replaces it wholesale. The sources live in `client/`.
src/HomeHub.Api/wwwroot/

# ---- Test / coverage ----
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/
coverage/
*.trx

# ---- Logs ----
*.log
logs/

# ---- Cached recipe images (Stage M2, meals-planning.md D5) ----
# Downloaded at import so a recipe card doesn't depend on someone else's CDN. Machine-local cache,
# content-addressed and re-fetchable, so it is not source. Deliberately NOT under wwwroot — that
# directory is the SPA build output and every deploy replaces it wholesale.
recipe-images/

# ---- Photographs read into calendar events (E3, event-capture.md D5/D6) ----
# The same reasoning as recipe-images above, and more sharply: these are photographs of the
# household's own post — a school flyer, a letter, a screenshot of somebody's text — kept against an
# engagement so it can be checked later. Machine-local, content-addressed, and emphatically not
# source. Without this line the first `git add -A` after somebody confirms a flyer commits a picture
# of their child's school letter to the repository, which is the exact disclosure this feature spends
# a privacy switch and a receipt line being careful about.
event-photos/

# ---- Local development TLS (scripts/make-dev-certs.sh) ----
# A private CA key that can sign for any hostname, plus the server key it signs. Both are secrets in
# the plain sense — anyone holding the CA key can mint a certificate the household's phones will
# trust without warning, because those phones have been told to trust this CA. Machine-local and
# regenerable in one command, so nothing is lost by never committing them.
certs/

# ---- OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# The dev CA, copied into public/ so a phone can download it from the dev server itself
# (deploy/dev-https.md §3). Public by nature — it is meant to be handed to devices — but
# machine-specific, so it is not source.
#
# Matched by name anywhere rather than at one path: `npm run build` copies everything in
# `client/public/` into `src/HomeHub.Api/wwwroot/`, so pinning the rule to the source location left
# the built copy untracked-and-committable. Delete it from `public/` once the household's devices
# are set up — otherwise every production build ships a development CA to a public URL.
homehub-dev-ca.crt

# /design-sync — staged converter scripts, build output, and machine-local state.
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
client/dist-ds/
.design-sync/.cache/
.design-sync/learnings/
.design-sync/node_modules

# The scratch-notes rule above ignores NOTES.md *anywhere*, which silently swallowed the sync's
# own handoff notes — the one file a future re-sync most needs. It is generated from this repo and
# the design project, never pasted into, so the secrets concern that rule guards against does not
# apply. Unignored by path so the blanket rule keeps protecting every other NOTES.md.
!.design-sync/NOTES.md

# ---- Claude Code local session state ----
# `settings.json` is the project's shared configuration and belongs in the repo. `settings.local.json`
# is one machine's permission allowlist, grown by whoever happened to be working there, and says
# nothing another checkout can use.
.claude/settings.local.json
